-===== arc snapshot --help =====
-Record the current branch head as a patchset with explicit base and brief binding. Accept preserves the delivered binding and contributor declaration through signature-only preparation; snapshots record evidence, never a judgment. A head whose rewrite invalidated approval requires a fresh patchset, even when the latest patchset's mapped head already matches the branch. Re-approval requires a verdict on that fresh patchset. Only the replay `arc rebase` performs itself records an inherited author: it carries the author coordinates of the patchset whose head it replayed, every contributor at its recorded model, and the replaying session is not its implementer. That replay runs where the project's configuration cannot define a merge driver or filter, and arc reads its result from the ref Git updated, not from command output. A snapshot, or the snapshot after a rebase that fell back to `git rebase` or stopped for resolution, records the head as its recorder's work unless `--on-behalf-of` or `--contributors` declares another author. At unchanged content, an explicit --on-behalf-of (also supplied by ARC_ON_BEHALF_OF) differing from the latest effective author records a fresh patchset. An equal or omitted subject preserves that patchset and its attribution; the unchanged output names the effective subject. Earlier verdicts remain bound to their original patchsets
-
