recovery. A hold release that names no active hold is the advice `hold-release-names-no-hold`; a change already reported with a problem is not checked for one. Under `[policy] review_clearance = "assessed"`, a debt it leaves owed that a read would discharge without it is the advice `clearance-keeps-debt-owed`, naming the change, the debt, that read and the debt's findings reads.
 
 Exits 0 when the ledger is clean or carries only advice, and 1 when it reports a problem. A ledger that cannot be read at all also exits 1, with the error on stderr and no report; a usage error exits 2. Records no events; ledger reads do not require a parseable append policy.
 
