 ===== arc cost show --help =====
-Report the work cost of a change, or of a journal artifact with its `supersedes` lineage and the changes begun from any name in it. Journal membership uses resolved journal and artifact identity: bare, qualified and equivalent directory spellings select the same work. References retain their original spelling as provenance. References outside a readable artifact's lineage need no resolution. Unavailable membership qualifies selection and withholds only dependent work totals; readable session figures remain available. Unreadable ledger records and published imports are coverage gaps beside readable peers. A query refuses only when neither target metadata nor any relevant dispatch or session can be read
+Report the work cost of a change, or of a journal artifact with its `supersedes` lineage and the changes begun from any name in it.
+
+Journal membership uses resolved journal and artifact identity: bare, qualified and equivalent directory spellings select the same work. References retain their original spelling as provenance. References outside a readable artifact's lineage need no resolution. Unavailable membership qualifies selection and withholds only dependent work totals; readable session figures remain available. Unreadable ledger records and published imports are coverage gaps beside readable peers. A query refuses only when neither target metadata nor any relevant dispatch or session can be read
 
 Each executor session bound to a selected run, and each participant, is measured through the pinned tapes reader over its whole recording, or, when the source is unavailable, from the facts `cost retain` kept, and the report says which. A fresh read that disagrees with facts retained at the same frontier shows the conflict. A session whose read failed and that no retained facts measure is unmeasured with `usage read failed`, or with `usage read failed transiently; a later read may succeed` where tapes found its store busy or unavailable through every attempt it makes. Direct totals count each undivided session whose work the item holds, and the item's share of each divided session with a span on it; inclusive totals for a change add the journal artifact it was begun from; the union counts each session once over the selection, a divided one by the selected items' shares. A run's figure is the segments that run alone covers. Every total names its quantity kind: the dollar figure a harness wrote is a harness-calculated estimate with an unknown pricing basis, a list-price estimate prices the disjoint categories by a `tapes-price-table/1` or `/2` table (`--prices`, else `TAPES_PRICES`, else `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tapes/prices.toml`) and the row of the model that served them, an event on a branch besides the active one by the model it names, a model's efforts priced together, a part no model is named for under uncertain attribution by no row, a figure one model served whole where its read leaves attribution uncertain with the unattributed-request reason, and a figure added up from segments by each segment's models, each share by its own recorded cache-write TTLs and reasons, never retained and absent with a reason when no table, model or row prices it. A `/2` row's long-context, time-of-day and validity terms are priced request by request from a fresh read, under the billing its recording establishes; retained facts hold no requests, so a term they could pay leaves a known su